</section>

<!-- Info Sections -->
<section class="container mb-5">
    <div class="row g-3">
        <section class="col-12 col-lg-6" id="what-is-json">
            <div class="p-4 bg-light border rounded h-100">
                <h2 class="mb-3">What is JSON?</h2>
                <div class="lead">
                    <p>
                        JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is a lightweight data-interchange format that
                        is easy for humans to read and write, and easy for machines to parse and
                        generate.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        It represents structured data using key-value pairs, arrays, and nested objects.
                        JSON is widely used in web development to exchange data between a client and a
                        server.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Despite its name, JSON is language-independent and supported by nearly all
                        modern programming languages including JavaScript, Python, PHP, Java, and more.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <h5>Example:</h5>
                <app-json-viewer [data]="exampleJson"></app-json-viewer>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="col-12 col-lg-6" id="why-json">
            <section class="p-4 bg-light border rounded h-100">
                <div class="container-fluid px-0">
                    <h2 class="mb-3">Why JSON?</h2>
                    <p class="lead mb-4">
                        JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is the universal format for structured data exchange on
                        the web. Here's why developers and systems around the world rely on it:
                    </p>
                    <div class="row gy-4">
                        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
                            <div class="p-4 border rounded bg-white shadow-sm h-100">
                                <h5>🌐 Human-Readable and Developer-Friendly</h5>
                                <p>JSON uses a simple structure of key-value pairs, making it easy to read, write,
                                    debug, and maintain.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
                            <div class="p-4 border rounded bg-white shadow-sm h-100">
                                <h5>⚡ Fast and Efficient</h5>
                                <p>With less overhead than formats like XML, JSON can be parsed and generated
                                    faster, using fewer resources — ideal for modern apps.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
                            <div class="p-4 border rounded bg-white shadow-sm h-100">
                                <h5>🔗 Backbone of REST APIs</h5>
                                <p>JSON is the standard for RESTful APIs. It enables seamless data transmission
                                    between client apps, servers, microservices, and more.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
                            <div class="p-4 border rounded bg-white shadow-sm h-100">
                                <h5>🔄 Language-Agnostic</h5>
                                <p>Supported by virtually all programming languages, JSON allows data exchange
                                    between diverse systems and platforms.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
                            <div class="p-4 border rounded bg-white shadow-sm h-100">
                                <h5>💾 Lightweight and Compact</h5>
                                <p>With minimal syntax and no extra markup, JSON reduces payload size — improving
                                    web and mobile app performance.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
                            <div class="p-4 border rounded bg-white shadow-sm h-100">
                                <h5>🧩 Perfect for Modern App Architectures</h5>
                                <p>JSON is a native fit for NoSQL databases, frontend frameworks (like React,
                                    Angular), and cloud-native tools (like Docker, Kubernetes).</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mt-4 p-4 bg-dark text-white rounded shadow">
                        <h4 class="mb-3">Why Use Our JSON Dev Tool?</h4>
                        <ul class="mb-0">
                            <li>✅ Format & Beautify Raw JSON</li>
                            <li>✅ Validate JSON Structures Instantly</li>
                            <li>✅ Use Dummy APIs for Testing</li>
                            <li>✅ Visualize JSON in Tree or Table View</li>
                            <li>✅ Import, Export & Convert JSON Easily</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>
        </section>
    </div>
</section>